meta {
  name: Upload Resume
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/resume
  body: multipartForm
  auth: inherit
}

body:multipart-form {
  resume: @file(/absolute/path/to/resume.pdf)
}

docs {
  # Upload Resume

  Admin only. Replaces the stored PDF — this is the whole update workflow, so
  there is no script and no env var to change.

  - `resume` must be a **PDF**, max **5 MB**. Use Bruno's file picker to replace
    the placeholder path.
  - The asset keeps a stable public id and is uploaded with `invalidate: true`,
    so the old file is purged from the CDN. The returned Cloudinary `version` is
    stored in `SiteAsset` and ends up in the download URL.

  Uploaded as `resource_type: raw`: Cloudinary blocks PDF delivery for `image`
  assets by default, so this must not be changed to `image`.

  | Status | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | 200 | replaced; `data.updatedAt` is when |
  | 400 | `RESUME_REQUIRED` or `UNSUPPORTED_RESUME_TYPE` |
  | 401 | missing or expired token |
  | 413 | `LIMIT_FILE_SIZE` — larger than 5 MB |
  | 503 | `CLOUDINARY_NOT_CONFIGURED` |
}
